hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"826","825 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jabir, on the authority of Busr bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, On the authority of Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not pray at graves, and do not sit on them.”"
"827","826 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, he said: I heard Al-Qasim speaking, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “There was a garment in my house that had pictures on it, so I put it on in a hurry in the house, so the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, praying to him, then he said: O Aisha, take it away from me, so I took it off and made it a pillow. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"828","827 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a mat that he would spread out during the day, and he would keep it at night and pray on it. So the people became aware of him, and they continued his prayer, and between him and them was the mat. He said: Do as much work as you are able, for God does not tire until you tire. And if a deed is dearest to God, he will do it consistently, even if it is small.” Then he left that place of prayer and did not return to it until God took him, and whenever he did a deed \"Prove it\""
"829","828 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a questioner asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “about praying in one garment, he said: Do you all have two garments?”"
"830","829 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, that he saw The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prays in one garment in Umm Salamah’s house, placing its two ends over his shoulders.”"
"831","830 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, he said: Anba Al-Attaf is Ibn Khalid, on the authority of Musa bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, he said: I said: : O Messenger of God, I am hunting and I only have a shirt on so I can pray in it? He said: “Put it on yourself, even if it is with a thorn.”"
"832","831 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Abu Hazim told me, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: “ There were men praying with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with their garments tied like boys, and the women were told, “Do not raise your heads until they are level.” The men are sitting.”"
"833","832 Shuaib bin Yusuf told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Anba Asim, on the authority of Amr bin Salamah, he said: “When my people returned from the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. They said: He said: Let the one among you who recites the Qur’an most recite the Qur’an lead you in prayer. He said: So they invited me and they taught me bowing and prostration, so I used to lead them in prayer. And there was a torn cloak on me, so they used to say to my father: Won’t you cover your son for us? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"834","833 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Waki’, he said: Talha bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray at night while I was beside him while I was menstruating, and I was wearing a cloak, part of it on the The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"835","834 Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu al-Zannad told us, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should pray in one garment, with nothing of it on his shoulders.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"836","835 Qutaibah bin Saeed and Issa bin Hammad informed us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba bin Amer said: “A silk robe was given as a gift to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he put it on, then prayed in it, then he left and took it off violently.” Like someone who hates it, then he said: “This is not appropriate for the righteous.”"
"837","836 Ishaq bin Ibrahim and Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He prayed in a khamisah that had signs, then he said: The signs of this one have occupied me, take it to my father.” Jahm, and bring me something prosperous.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"838","837 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfah, on the authority of his father, The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He came out in a red robe and set upon a goat and prayed to it, behind which the dog and the woman passed. And the donkey (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"839","838 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Hisham bin Abdul Malik told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Jabir told me Ibn Subh, he said: I heard Khalas Ibn Amr, saying: I heard Aisha, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I were in Abu al-Qasim. The one slogan: I am menstruating and menstruating, so if any of my semen gets on him, he washes off what got to him and does not return it to anyone else, and prays in it, then comes back with me. If something from me befalls him and he does something like that, he will not do it again.”"
"840","839 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, He said: “I saw Jarir urinate, then he called for water, performed ablution, and wiped over his socks, then he got up and prayed, and he was asked about that, and he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He did something like that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"841","840 Amr bin Ali informed us, on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, and Ghassan bin Mudar, a trustworthy Basri, who said: Abu Maslamah told us He is Saeed bin Yazid. He said: I asked Anas, “Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray in sandals?” He said: Yes."
"842","841 Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id and Shu`aib ibn Yusuf informed us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad informed me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He prayed on the day of the conquest and placed his shoes on the \"His left\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"843","842 Ishaq bin Ibrahim and Hannad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Hussein bin Ali Al-Jafi, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zar, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested, the Ansar said: From us is a leader and from you is a leader, so Omar came to them and said : Do you not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer? Which of you would be willing to lead the people in prayer? Is Abu Bakr advancing? They said: We seek refuge in God lest we advance Abu Bakr."
"844","843 Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ismail bin Aliya told us, he said: Abba Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah Al-Baraa, he said: Delayed Ibn al-Samit came to me, so I threw a chair for him, and he sat on it. I mentioned to him what Ziyad had done to him, so he bit his lip and hit my thigh, and said: I asked Abu Dharr about what you asked me, and he struck my thigh just as I struck your thigh, and he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. As you asked me, he struck my thigh just as I struck your thigh, and said: “Pray the prayer at its time. If I overtake you with them, pray, and do not say, ‘I prayed,’” \"I pray\""
"845","844 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja’, on the authority of Aws bin Damaj, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The people who are most literate in the Book of God will lead the people in prayer, if they are equal in recitation.” So he was the oldest of them in the migration, and if they were the same in the migration, then he is the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah, and if they were the same in the Sunnah, then the oldest of them in the migration, and no “You shall lead a man while he is under his authority, and you shall not sit as his guest in his house unless he gives you permission.”"
"846","845 Hajib bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Malik bin al-Huwayrith, He said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, me and a cousin of mine, and he once said: Me and a friend of mine, and he said: “If you travel, give us the call to prayer and stay.” And let the eldest of you lead you in prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"847","846 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Hisham, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Saeed, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If there are three of them, let one of them lead them, and the most worthy of the imamate is the one closest to them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"848","847 Ibrahim bin Muhammad told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja’, on the authority of Aws bin Damaj, on the authority of Abu Masoud, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man should not lead in prayer while in his power, nor should he sit in his honor except \"With His permission\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"849","848 Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Sa’d, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He received word that there was something going on between the Banu Amr bin Awf, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to reconcile among them among some people with him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was imprisoned, and the time for prayer came, so Bilal came to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, has been imprisoned and the time for prayer has come, so can you lead the people? He said: Yes, if you wish. So Bilal stood up, and Abu Bakr came forward and said “Allahu Akbar” to the people. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and walked in the rows until he stood up. row, and the people began to applaud, and Abu Bakr did not turn around during his prayer, but when the people increased, he turned around, and saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pointed to him, ordering him to pray, so Abu Bakr raised his hands, and he thanked God, and the retreating man returned after him. Until he stood in line, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came forward and prayed for the people. When he finished, he approached the people and said: O people, “What Mind you, when something bothers you during prayer, you begin to applaud. The applause is for women. Whoever is disturbed by something during his prayer, let him say, Glory be to God, for he does not Someone hears him when he says: Glory be to God, unless you turn around, O Abu Bakr, what prevented you from leading the people in prayer when I indicated to you? Then Abu Bakr said: Ibn Abi Quhafa should not have come before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"850","849 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The last prayer prayed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, he prayed with the people in one garment, wearing his robe, behind Abu Bakr.”"
"851","850 Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna informed us, saying: Bakr ibn Issa told me, saying: I heard Shu’bah, mentioned, on the authority of Nu’aym ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, “Abu Bakr led the people in prayer while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the people in prayer in the row.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"852","851 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Anba Abdullah, on the authority of Aban bin Yazid, he said: Badil bin Maysarah told us, he said: Abu told us Atiyya, a servant of ours, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwaith, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If one of you visits a people, do not They pray with them.”"
"853","852 Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Maan told us, he said: Malik told us. H said: And I am Al-Harith bin Miskin, reciting to him, and I am listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’, that Itban bin Malik “He used to lead his people in prayer while he was blind, and he said: O Messenger of God, it is darkness, the rain and the torrent, and I A blind man. He prayed, O Messenger of God, in my house, a place that he used as a place of prayer. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: Where do you like? Should I pray? He pointed to a place in the house, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed there."
"854","853 Musa bin Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi al-Kufi informed us, saying: Husayn bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayoub. He said: Amr bin Salamah Al-Jarmi told me, he said: The riders used to pass by us and we would learn the Qur’an from them, so he came to my father, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted you and said: “The one who recites the Qur’an most of you will lead you in prayer.” Then my father came and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He will lead you in prayer.” I am the one who recited the Qur’an the most. So they looked and I was the one who recited the Qur’an the most, so I used to lead them in prayer, and I was eight years old.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"855","854 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Abi Abdullah, and Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When prayer is called, do not Arise until you see me.”"
"856","855 Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “Prayer was established while the Messenger of God “A man was saved, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he did not stand up to pray until the people fell asleep.”"
"857","856 Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir told us, he said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and he told us Al-Walid, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The prayer was performed and the people formed their rows, and the Messenger of God came out God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, even when he stood up in his place of prayer, he mentioned that he had not washed, so he said to the people: Where are you? Then he returned to his house and left. “It is upon Us that he clean his head after he has bathed, and we are in ranks.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"858","857 Ahmad bin Abdah informed us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, and mentioned a word that means it. Abu Hazim told us, saying: Sahl bin Saad said: There was a fight between Banu Amr bin Awf, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard of this, so he prayed the noon prayer, then he came to them to reconcile between them, then he said To Bilal: “O Bilal, when the afternoon prayer comes and I do not come, then order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” When I arrived, Bilal called the call to prayer, then stayed, and said to Abu Bakr: He advanced, and Abu Bakr advanced, and entered into the prayer, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and began to divide the people until he stood behind Abu Bakr. He applauded the people, and when Abu Bakr entered the prayer he did not turn around, so when Abu Bakr saw that the applaud was not held back, he turned around and nodded. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him with his hand, and he thanked God for the saying of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Go ahead.” Then Abu walked away. Bakr Al-Qahqari walked on his heels and delayed. When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw that, he came forward and led the people in prayer, and when he finished his prayer, he said: “ O Abu Bakr, what prevented you when I motioned to you, did you not go ahead?” He said: It was not for Ibn Abi Quhafa to lead the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, and he said to the people: “If something bothers you, let the men praise Him, and let the women praise Him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"859","858 Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell from a horse on its side. The right hand, so they entered upon it and returned to it, and the time for prayer came. When he finished the prayer, he said: “The imam is only to be followed, so when he bows, they bow, and when He raised, so raise up, and when he prostrates, prostrate, and when he says: God hears those who praise Him, then say: Our Lord, praise be to You.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"860","859 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah, meaning bin Al-Mubarak, told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Hayyan, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw his companions delaying, so he said: “Come forward and follow me, and let those who follow you follow me.” After you, and a people will continue to delay until God delays them.” Anba Suwayd bin Nasr, who said: Anba Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, etc (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"861","860 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told me, he said: Anba Shu’bah, on the authority of Musa Ibn Abi Aisha, he said: I heard Ubaid God bin Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “ordered Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” She said: And it was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the presence of Abu Bakr, so he prayed sitting while Abu Bakr led the people in prayer, and the people were behind Abu Bakr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"862","861 Ubayd Allah ibn Fadala ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abba Yahya, meaning Ibn Yahya, he said: Abba Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Humaid al-Ru’asi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer at Dhuhr and Abu Bakr. Behind him, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Allahu Akbar,” Abu Bakr said “Allahu Akbar,” so he would listen to us."
"863","862 Muhammad ibn Ubaid informed us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Harun ibn Antara, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of al-Aswad And Alqamah, they said: We entered upon Abdullah at midday, and he said: “There will be princes who will be distracted from the time of prayer, so pray it at its time. Then he got up and prayed between me and him, and said: This is what I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"864","863 Abdah bin Abdullah told us, he said: Abba Zaid, he said: Aflah bin Saeed told us, he said: Buraydah bin Sufyan bin Farwa Al-Aslami, on the authority of a boy of his grandfather, called Masoud, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr passed by me, and Abu Bakr said to me Bakr: O Masoud, go to Abu Tamim, meaning his master, and tell him to carry us on a camel and send us provisions and a guide to guide us. So I came. To my master, so I informed him, and he sent with me a camel and bricks of milk, so I began to take them to hide the way, and the time for prayer came.” Then the Messenger stood up. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He was praying, and Abu Bakr stood to his right. I had learned about Islam while I was with them, so I came and stood behind them, so he pushed The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the chest of Abu Bakr, so we stood behind him.”"
"865","864 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that his grandmother Mulaika invited the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to eat some food she had prepared, and he ate from it. Then he said: “Get up, so I will lead you in prayer.” Anas said: So I got up to “A mat of ours had turned black from long wear, so I sprinkled it with water.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, and the orphan and I lined up behind him. The old man was behind us, so he prayed two rak’ahs for us and then left.”"
"866","865 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Sulayman bin al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: “A messenger entered upon us. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and it is only me, my mother, and Umm Haram, my aunt. He said: “Get up, so I will lead you in prayer.” He said: At a time other than prayer. He said: So he led us in prayer"
"867","866 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Mukhtar speaking, on the authority of Musa Ibn Anas, on the authority of Anas, that it was him and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his mother and aunt, “So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed So he placed Anas on his right, and his mother and aunt behind them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"868","867 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Musa bin Anas, on the authority of Anas said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led in prayer with me and a woman from my family, so he made me stand on his right, and the woman was behind us.”"
"869","868 Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of his father On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I was with my aunt Maimunah. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and prayed during the night, so I stood to his left. Then he said to me thus, and he took hold of my head and set me on his right hand.”"
"870","869 Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wipe our shoulders during prayer, and say: “Do not disagree, lest your hearts disagree. How beautiful among you are those who have dreams.” And the prohibition, then those after them, then those after them.” Abu Masoud said: Today you are more in disagreement."
"871","870 Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali bin Muqaddam told us, he said: Yusuf bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad said: “While I was in the mosque in Medina in the front row, a man pulled me from behind me, leaning down and standing in my place. By God, I did not understand my prayer. When he left, it was Ubayy bin Ka’b, and he said: O boy, may God not cause you harm. This is a covenant from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He asked us to follow him, then he faced the Qiblah and said: “The people of Al-Aqd and the Lord of the Kaaba have perished three times.” Then he said: “By God, “I am sorry for them, but I am sorry for those whom they have led astray.” I said: “O Abu Ya’qub, what do you mean by the people of the contract?” He said: “the princes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"872","871 Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abd informed me The Most Gracious, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The prayer was established, so we stood up and the rows were straightened before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us. And peace be upon him, “Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came until he had stood up in his place of prayer before he said the takbir, then he left, and said to us: Where are you? He came down to stand and we waited for him until he came out to us. He had bathed, rinsing his head with water, then he said the takbir and prayed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"873","872 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, May God bless him and grant him peace. He straightened the rows as you straighten a cup. Then I saw a man with his chest coming out of the row. I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: That you may straighten your ranks, or God will cause discord between your faces.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"874","873 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, On the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pass through the row from one side to the other, wiping our shoulders. And our chests, and He says: “Do not differ, lest your hearts differ.” And He used to say: “Indeed, God and His angels pray in the front rows.”"
"875","874 Bishr bin Khalid informed us, he said: Anba Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abu Masoud said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wipe our shoulders and say: “Stay equal, and do not differ lest your hearts differ, but let me be gentle.” “Among you are those who are first of dreams and prohibitions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them.”"
"876","875 Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Nafi’ Basri informed us, saying: Anba Bahz bin Asad said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “Stay, stay, stay, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I see you from behind me, as I see you.” \"In my hands\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"877","876 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Anba Ismail, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us. On his face when he stood up to pray before saying the “Allahu Akbar,” he said: “Straighten your rows and close together, for I see you behind my back.”"
"878","877 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, he said: Aban told us, he said: Qatada told us, he said: Anas told us that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Compose your ranks and keep your necks together.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"879","878 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim, who is Ibn Tarfa, On the authority of Jabir bin Samurah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us and said: “Don’t you line up as the angels line up before their Lord?” They said: How do the angels line up before their Lord? He said: “They complete the first row, and stand together in the row.”"
"880","879 Yahya bin Othman Al-Homsi told us, saying: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Buhair bin Saad, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Jubayr Bin Nufayr, on the authority of Irbad bin Sariyah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to “pray three times in the first row, and one in the second row.”"
"881","880 Ismail bin Masoud told us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Complete the first row, then the next. If there is a deficiency, let it be in the back row.”"
"882","881 Issa bin Ibrahim bin Matrud told us, there is nothing wrong with him, he said: Abdullah bin Wahb told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Kathir ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever joins a line, may God bless him.” And whoever cuts a line, God will cut him off.”"
"883","882 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Jarir, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “The best rows for men are the first, and the worst are the last, and the best rows for women are the last, and the worst are the first.”"
"884","883 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Hani, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Mahmoud, he said: We were with Anas and we prayed with one of the princes, so they pushed us until we stood between the two pillars, so Anas made to delay, and said: “We have We used to fear this during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"885","884 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Anba Abdullah, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ibn al-Bara’, on the authority of al-Bara’, he said: We used to say, “When we prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I liked to be at his right.”"
"886","885 Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “If one of you leads people in prayer, let him make it short, for among them are the sick, the weak, and the old, and if one of you prays for himself, let him make it as long as he wants.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"887","886 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “ “The people are the easiest to pray completely.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"888","887 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abu Qatada, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I stand up for prayer and hear the child crying, so I continue in my prayer.” “I hate to make it difficult for his mother.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"889","888 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled, who is Ibn Al-Harith, told us on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: Al-Harith told me Ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Salim Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to command us with lightness and makes us believe in the pure ones.”"
"890","889 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, On the authority of Amr bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, leading the people in prayer while he was pregnant with Umamah, the daughter of Abu Al-Aas. upon himself, so when he bows he places it, and when he finishes his prostration he repeats it.”"
"891","890 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “Doesn’t the one who raises his head before the imam fear that God will turn his head into the head of a donkey?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"892","891 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Anba Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Yazid, delivering a sermon, said: Al-Baraa narrated to us, and he was not lying, that they used to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he raised his head from bowing, they stand until they see him prostrating, then they prostrate.”"
"893","892 Mu’mal bin Hisham informed us, saying: Abba Ismail, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah He said: Abu Musa led us in prayer. When he was sitting, a man from the people said: Prayer was established with righteousness and zakat. So when Abu Musa said the salutation, he went to The people, so he said: Which of you said this word and insulted the people? He said: Oh Hattan, perhaps you said it? I said: No, and I was afraid that you would swallow me up with it. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us our prayers and our Sunnahs, so he said: “Only The imam is to be followed, so when he says “Allahu Akbar”, so do “Allahu Akbar”, and when he says: “Not upon whom is anger nor gone astray” then say: “Ameen”, may God answer you. He bowed, so they bowed, and when he rose, he said: God hears those who praise Him, so say: Our Lord, praise be to You, God hears you. So when he prostrated So prostrate, and when he rises, rise up, for the imam prostrates before you and rises before you.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So that is \"With that\""
"894","893 Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “He came A man from the Ansar, and the prayer was being held, entered the mosque and prayed behind Muadh, and he continued with them. The man left and prayed in the direction of the mosque, then he set off. When Muadh finished the prayer, he was told: So-and-so did such-and-such, and Muadh said: If I wake up in the morning, I will mention that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he mentioned that to him, so he sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “What made you do what you did?” He said: O Messenger of God, I worked during the daytime, so I came and the prayer had been established, so I entered the mosque and joined with him in prayer, and he recited Surah Such and such, and it took a long time, so I left and prayed near the mosque, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let us be tempted, O Muadh! Let us be tempted, O Muadh! \"Moaz\""
"895","894 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He rode a horse and it fell from its right side, so he prayed one of the prayers while sitting, and we prayed behind him while sitting, and when he left, he said: The imam was appointed to be followed, so when he prays standing, they should pray standing, and when he bows, then kneel, and when he says: God hears those who praise Him, So say: Our Lord, and to You be praise. And when he prays sitting, pray sitting all together.”"
"896","895 Abu Kurayb Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, saying: Abu Muawiyah reported, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became heavy, Bilal came to call him to prayer, and he said: ‘Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.’” She said: So I said: O Messenger of God, Abu Bakr is a tough man, and when he takes your place, the people will not listen. If you had ordered Omar, he would have said: “Tell Abu Bakr, let him lead the people in prayer.” So I said to Hafsa: “Tell him.” She said to him, and he said: “Indeed, you are the companions of Joseph. Go to Abu Bakr.” Let him lead the people in prayer.” She said: So they ordered Abu Bakr, and when he entered the prayer, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, found lightness in himself. She said: So he stood, being guided between two men, and his feet were stepping on the ground. She said: When he entered the mosque, Abu Bakr heard his senses, so he went to be late. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, motioned to him, “Get up as you are.” She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came until he got up. Abu Bakr left, sitting, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading the people in prayer, sitting while Abu Bakr was standing. Abu Bakr followed the example of the Messenger May God bless him and grant him peace, and people follow the example of Abu Bakr. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"897","896 Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Abdul-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Zaida told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, who said: I entered upon Aisha and said: Don’t you tell me about the illness of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? ? She said: “Yes.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became heavy and said: “Did the people pray?” So we said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of God. He said: “Put water for me in the basin.” So we did so, so he washed, then he went to get some water. He fainted, then he woke up and said: “Did the people pray?” We said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of God. The third said the same as he said. She said: And the people are sitting in the mosque waiting for the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, for the evening prayer, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent for Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer, and he came to him. The Messenger, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commands you to lead the people in prayer. Abu Bakr was a gentle man, so he said: O Omar, pray. With the people, he said: You have more right to that, so Abu Bakr led them in prayer in those days, and then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, found some He felt lightness himself, so he came to be guided between two men, one of whom was Al-Abbas, for the noon prayer. When Abu Bakr saw him, he went to stay behind, so he nodded. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him not to delay, and he ordered them to make him sit next to him, so he made Abu Bakr pray standing. And the people prayed with the prayer of Abu Bakr, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed while sitting. So I entered upon Ibn Abbas and said: Shall I not offer you What did Aisha tell me about the illness of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, so I told him, and he did not deny anything about it, except that he said: She named for you the man who was with Abbas? I said: No. He said: He is Ali. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Musa bin Abi Aisha, trustworthy. Sufyan al-Thawri used to praise Musa bin Abu Aisha, he is Kufa"
"898","897 Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, saying: “Muadh was praying With the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he returned to his people and led them in prayer. One night he delayed the prayer and prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he returned to his people, leading them, and recited Surat Al-Baqarah. When a man from the people heard that, he delayed and prayed, then left, and they said: You hypocritically, O so-and-so, and he said: By God, I did not hypocrite. I would have come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him. So he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of God, Muadh prays with you, then he comes and leads us, and you delayed the prayer yesterday, so he prayed with you, then he came back and we were safe. So he opened Surat Al-Baqarah, and when I heard that, I delayed and prayed, but we are the owners of clearings and we work with our hands, so the Prophet said to him, “Pray.” May God bless him and grant him peace: “O Muadh, are you tempted? Recite such-and-such surah and such-and-such surah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"899","898 Bishr bin Hilal told us, he said: Yahya al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, “He prayed the prayer of fear, and he prayed two rak’ahs for those behind him, and two rak’ahs for those who came, so it was for the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” He said salutations four times, and for them and for them he performed two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"900","899 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Prayer “The congregational prayer is twenty-seven degrees superior to the single prayer.”"
"901","900 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “A congregational prayer is twenty-five times better than the prayer of one of you alone.”"
"902","901 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ammar, he said: Al-Qasim bin Muhammad told me On the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The congregational prayer is twenty-five degrees greater than the individual prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"903","902 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If there are three of them, let one of them lead them, and the most worthy of the Imamate is the one closest to them.”"
"904","903 Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Ziyad told me that Qaza’ah A servant of Abdul Qais told him that he heard Ikrimah say: Ibn Abbas said: “I prayed next to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Aisha is behind us, praying with us, and I am next to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying with him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"905","905 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Sulayman, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “I prayed One night with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I stood on his left and he took me with his left hand until he made me stand on his right.”"
"906","906 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled, who is Ibn Al-Harith, told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that He told them on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Basir, on the authority of his father. Shu’bah said: And Abu Ishaq said, and I heard it from him and from his father, He said: I heard Ubayy bin Ka’b saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the morning prayer, and he said: “Did so-and-so witness the prayer?” They said: No. He said: “ “So-and-so?” They said: No. He said: “Indeed, these two prayers are among the heaviest prayers for the hypocrites, and if they knew what is in them, they would have performed them even if they were crawling.” And the row. The first is like a row of angels, and if you knew his virtue, you would hasten to him, and a man’s prayer with another man is purer than his prayer alone, and the prayer of a man with another man is purer than his prayer alone. A man’s prayer with two men is purer than his prayer with another man, and the more they are, the more beloved he is to God.”"
"907",""
"908","908 Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Zubayd, whose name is Abther bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of His father, he said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when some people said: If you attack us, O Messenger of God,” he said: “I am afraid If you sleep while missing the prayer, then Bilal said: I will protect you. So they lay down and fell asleep, and Bilal leaned his back against his camel, and the Messenger of God woke up. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, meaning the visor of the sun had risen, and he said: “O Bilal, where is what you said?” He said: I have never been subjected to a sleep like this. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God has taken your souls when He willed and restored them.” Whenever he wanted, stand up, O Bilal, and call the people to prayer.” So Bilal stood up and called for prayer, and they performed ablutions, meaning when the sun rose, then he stood up and led them in prayer."
"909","909 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Zaida bin Qadamah, he said: Al-Sa’ib bin Hubaysh Al-Kala’i told us, on the authority of Ma’dan bin Abi Talha Al-Amari said: Abu Al-Darda’ said to me: Where is your residence? So I said: In the village of Duwayn Homs. Abu Darda’ said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There are not three in a village nor Bedouins among whom prayer is not performed unless Satan has taken control of them, so you must perform in congregation, for the wolf only devours the stray animal.” Al-Sa’ib said: meaning In congregation in congregation in prayer"
"910","910 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I was about to order a firewood to be gathered, then to order the prayer to be announced, then to order a man to lead the prayer.” people, then I will go to men and burn their houses, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if one of them knew that he would find a fat bone or “Two beautiful throws for the evening meal.”"
"911","911 Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, saying: Anba Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas On the authority of Abdullah, he used to say: “Whoever is pleased to meet God in peace tomorrow, let him observe these five daily prayers whenever he is called to them.” For God has established for His Prophet the laws of guidance, and they are among the laws of guidance, and I do not consider that any of you does not have a mosque in which he prays in his house. If you prayed in your homes and left your mosques, you would have abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet, and if you had abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet, you would have gone astray, and no servant A Muslim performs ablution and does it well, then walks to prayer, except that God records for him a good deed for every step he takes, or raises him for it for it. To a degree, or his sin will be atoned for by it. You have seen us approaching the error, and you have seen us, and no one lags behind except a known hypocrite. His hypocrisy, and I saw a man being guided between two men until he stood in line.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"912","912 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Al-Asam told us, on the authority of his uncle Yazid bin Al-Asam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “A blind man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I have no guide to lead me to Prayer, so he asked him if he would be given permission to pray in his house, so he granted him permission. When he left, he called him and said to him: “Do you hear the call to prayer? He said: Yes. He said: Answer him."
"913","Harun bin Zaid bin Yazid bin Abi Al-Zarqa told us, my father told us, he said: Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Qasim bin Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abis, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila, on the authority of Ibn Umm Maktoum, he said: O Messenger of God, “The city is full of vermin and wild beasts.” So he said: Do you hear my command to pray? He greeted the farmer. He said: Yes. He said: He greeted the farmer. He was not given a permit. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"914","914 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, that Abdullah bin Arqam used to lead One day, the time for prayer came, so he went to fulfill his needs, then came back and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If he finds If one of you excretes, let him cleanse it before praying.”"
"915","915 Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Abba Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If Dinner has been prepared and prayer has been established, so begin with dinner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"916","916 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of His father, he said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Hunayn, when rain hit us, and the herald of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called out: “Pray in your travels.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"917","917 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, saying: Abba Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Tahla, on the authority of Muhsin bin Ali al-Fihri, on the authority of Awf bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs ablution, performs it well, then goes out “If he goes to the mosque and finds the people praying, God will record for him a reward similar to the one who attended it, and that will not detract from their rewards in the slightest.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"918","918 Suleiman bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Al-Hakim bin Abdullah Al-Qurashi narrated to him Nafi’ bin Jubayr and Abdullah bin Abi Salamah told him, that Muadh bin Abdul Rahman told them, on the authority of Hamran, the client of Uthman. On the authority of Othman bin Affan, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever performs ablution for prayer and performs the ablution thoroughly and then walks To the prescribed prayer, and he prays it with the people, or with the congregation, or in the mosque, his sin will be forgiven.”"
"919","919 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of a man from Banu Ad-Dail called Busr bin Muhjan, on the authority of Muhjan, that he was in a session with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the call to prayer was called, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, and then He returned and was sitting in a state of distress, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “What prevented you from praying? Aren’t you a Muslim man?” He said: Yes, But I had prayed with my family, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “If you come, pray with the people, even if you have already prayed.”"
"920","920 Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Anba Ya’la bin Ata’, he said: Jabir bin Yazid bin Al-Aswad told us. Al-Amiri, on the authority of his father, said: I witnessed the dawn prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Al-Khaif Mosque. When he finished his prayer, he Two men at the back of the people did not pray with him, so he said: “I have to do so.” So they were brought while their horses were thundering, and he said: “What prevented you from praying?” With us? They said: O Messenger of God, we have prayed in our camps. He said: So do not do that. If you prayed in your camps and then came to a mosque in congregation. So pray with them, for it is a voluntary prayer for you.”"
"921","921 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala and Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Khaled, who is Ibn Al-Harith, he said: He told us Shu`bah, on the authority of Badil, he said: I heard Abu Al-Aliyah narrating, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me May God bless him and grant him peace, and he struck my thigh: “How will you fare if you remain among a people who delay prayer beyond its appointed time?” I said: What do you command? He said: “Pray the prayer at its appointed time, then go for your need. If the prayer is performed while you are in a mosque, then pray.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"922","922 Ibrahim bin Muhammad told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Suleiman Maimunah's servant, he said: I saw Ibn Umar sitting on the court and people were praying, I said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, why are you not praying? He said: I have prayed. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Prayer should not be repeated twice in a day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"923","923 Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you come to prayer, do not come to it running, but come to it running calmly over you, so whatever you catch up with, pray. And whatever you miss, make up for it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"924","924 Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr told us, he said: Anba Ibn Wahb, he said: Anba Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Outcast, on the authority of Al-Fadl. Ibn Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prayed the afternoon prayer, he would go to Bani Abd al-Ashhal. Then he would talk to them until he descended to Morocco. Abu Rafi’ said: While the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was hastening to Morocco, we passed by. At Al-Baqi’, he said: “Father to you, afflicted by you.” He said: Then that grew on my arm, so I delayed, and I thought he wanted me to go, so he said: “What’s the matter with you?” Walk.” I said: Did I cause something to happen? He said: “What is that?” “I said: Did you show me some respect?” He said: “No, but this is so-and-so whom I sent to hunt down the sons of so-and-so, and he tied up a number, and now he is covered with a similar amount of fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"925","925 Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Othman told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah bin told me Abdul Rahman and Abu Abdullah Al-Aghar, that Abu Hurairah told them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is only a parable The one who migrates to prayer is like the one who guides a camel, then the one who follows it is like the one who guides a cow, then the one who follows it is like the one who guides “The ram, then the one who follows it is like the one who guides the hen, then the one who follows it is like the one who guides the egg.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"926","926 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abba Abdullah, who is Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Zakaria, he said: Amr bin Dinar told me, he said: I heard Ata’ bin Yassar speaking, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the prayer is established, then there is no prayer except \"the written\""
"927","927 Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, saying: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Warqa’ Ibn Umar, on the authority of Amr Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “When the establishment of prayer is There is no prayer except the prescribed ones.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"928","928 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim, on the authority of Ibn At one point, he said: “The morning prayer was established, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man praying and the muezzin was standing, so he said: Do you pray the morning prayer for four days?”"
"929","929 Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Asim told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sarjis, he said: “He came A man and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were in the morning prayer, so he prayed two rak'ahs, then he entered, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished his prayer, He said: O so-and-so, which is the prayer that you prayed with us or the one that you prayed for yourself?"
"930","930 Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Ishaq bin Abdullah told me, he said: I heard Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to our house, and I and an orphan of ours prayed behind him, and Umm Sulaym prayed behind us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"931","931 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Nuh, meaning Ibn Qays, told us, on the authority of Ibn Malik, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He is Amr bin Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Jawza, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “A beautiful woman was praying behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The best of people said: Some people would move forward in the first row so that they would not see her, and some of them would delay until they were in the back row. He bowed down, meaning he looked under his armpit, so God revealed “And We knew those who came forward among you, and We knew those who would come later.”"
"932","932 Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ziyad the most knowledgeable, he said: Al-Hasan told us, Abu Bakra told him that he “entered the mosque and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was bowing, so he kneeled without the row.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “May God increase your eagerness, and do not repeat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"933","933 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, saying: Abu Usama told me, he said: Al-Walid bin Kathir told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abu Sa`id, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed one day, then he left and said: O so-and-so, didn’t You pray well, so that the one praying does not think about how he is praying for himself, for I see from behind me as I see from before me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"934","934 Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ibrahim informed us, saying: Our name is Ishaq, meaning ibn Yusuf al-Azraq, on the authority of Zakaria ibn Abi Zaida, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Aazib, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and prayed with Nahu and the Holy House for sixteen months, then He was directed to the Kaaba, and a man who had prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace over a group of the Ansar, passed by and said: “I bear witness that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was directed to the Kaaba, so they turned to the Kaaba.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"935","935 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And he said hello, “He prays on his camel while traveling wherever it is headed.” Malik said: Abdullah bin Dinar said, and Ibn Umar used to do that."
"936","936 Issa bin Hammad informed us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb. He said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would say the tasbih over a camel animal before any direction he went, and say the Witr prayer over it, but he would not pray over it the prescribed prayer.”"
"937","937 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, who said: While the people were in Quba’ in The morning prayer. A man came to them and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was revealed to him tonight, and he was commanded to face the Qiblah. So they faced it, and their faces were towards the Levant, so they turned to the Kaaba.”"
"938","938 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib bin Abi Hamza told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Salem told me And Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Homsi told us, he said: Othman told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar told me, On the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “When he opened the takbeer in the prayer, he raised his hands when he said the takbeer, so that He makes them equal to his shoulders, and when he says the takbir for bowing, he does the same, then when he says: God hears those who praise Him, he does the same. And he said: Our Lord, praise be to You, and he does not do that when he prostrates, nor when he raises his head from prostration. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"939","939 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah and he is Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Salem informed me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he stood for prayer, raising his hands until they were level with his shoulders, then he would say “Allahu Akbar.” He said: He used to do that when he said the takbir when bowing, and he would do that when he raised his head from bowing, and he would say: God hears those who praise Him, and He does not He does that while prostrating.\""
"940","940 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, used to say: “When he began the prayer, he raised his hands at the level of his shoulders, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, he raised them in the same way, and he said “God hears whoever praises Him. Our Lord, praise be to You.” He did not do that when prostrating."
"941","941 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father, he said: I prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he opened the prayer, he said “Allahu Akbar” and raised his hands until they were close to his ears, then he recited the opening of the book, When he finished it, he said: Amen, extending his voice with it."
"942","942 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Nasr bin Asim, on the authority of Malik Ibn Al-Huwayrith, who was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prayed, he raised his hands when He says “Allahu Akbar” near his ears, when he wants to bow, and when he raises his head from bowing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"943","943 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Ibn Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Nasr bin Asim, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwayrith said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he entered into prayer, raising his hands, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, until the branches of his ears were aligned.”"
"944","944 Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Fitr bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abd al-Jabbar bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father He saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he opened the prayer, he raised his hands until his thumbs were almost parallel to the lobes of his ears,” Abu Abd said. Al-Rahman: Abdul-Jabbar bin Wael did not hear from his father, and the hadith itself is authentic. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"945","945 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, he said: Sa`id bin Samaan told me, he said: Abu came Hurairah went to the Mosque of Banu Zurayk and said: “There are three things that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do, but people abandoned them: He used to raise his hands in prayer.” He extended his voice, was silent for a moment, and said “Allahu Akbar” when he prostrated and when he bowed.”"
"946","946 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father. Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered the mosque, and a man entered and prayed, then he came and greeted the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, replied to him and said: “Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” So he went back and prayed as he had prayed, then he came to The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, greeted him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “And peace be upon you, go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” So he did. That was three times, then the man said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I am not better than this, so teach me. He said: “When you stand up to pray, say the takbir, then Recite what is easy for you from the Qur’an, then bow until you are at ease, then rise until you are standing upright, then prostrate until you are at ease. Prostrating, then rise until you are comfortable sitting, then do that throughout your entire prayer.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He succeeded Yahya on this matter. The hadith, and it was said: On the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and the hadith is authentic. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"947","947 Muhammad bin Wahb told us, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahim, he said: Zaid told me, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, said: “A man stood up behind the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: God is great, great. Praise be to God a lot, and Glory be to God tomorrow and the evening. Then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Who is the one who spoke the word?” Then a man said: It is me, O Messenger of God. He said: Twelve kings took the initiative to do so. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"948","948 Muhammad bin Shuja’ told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: “While we were praying with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man from the people said: God is most great, praise be to God greatly. Glory be to God, morning and evening. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who said such-and-such a word?” Then a man from among the people said: It is me, O Messenger of God. He said: “I was amazed at her and he mentioned a word that meant it. The gates of heaven were opened for her,” he said. Ibn Umar: I have not abandoned it since I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"949","949 Suwayd bin Nasr Al-Marwazi informed us, saying: I am Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Musa bin Umair Al-Anbari, and Qays, saying: Na Alqamah bin Wael, on the authority of his father, said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “When he was standing during prayer, he would hold his right hand over his left.”"
"950","950 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Abi Zainab, he said: I heard Abu Uthman He narrates, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw me and I had placed my left hand on my right during prayer, so he took my right hand and placed it on Northern.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: No one sent this hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"951","951 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Zaida, he said: Asim bin Kulayb told us, he said: My father told me, That Wael bin Hajar told him, saying: I said to look at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, how he prays, so I looked at him, so he stood up and said the takbir, He raised his hands until they were close to his ears, then he placed his right hand on his left palm, wrist and forearm, then when he wanted to bow, he raised His hands are like it.” He said: “And he placed his hands on his knees, then when he raised his head, he raised his hands like it, then he prostrated and placed his palms on his sandals.” his ears, then he sat and spread his left leg, and placed his left palm on his left thigh and knee, and placed the edge of his right elbow on So he took his right thigh, then he clenched two of his fingers and circled it, then he raised his finger, and I saw him move it and make supplication with it.”"
"952","952 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Hisham, and Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: I am the servant of God, and the pronunciation is for him. On the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade a man to pray shortened,” Abu Abd said. The Most Gracious: Other than Hisham, he said in this hadith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he forbade a man to pray (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"953","953 Humayd ibn Masada informed us, on the authority of Sufyan ibn Habib, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Subayh, who said: “I prayed beside Ibn Omar, so I put my hands on my waist, and he said to me: Thus, he struck him with his hand. When I prayed, I said to a man: Who is this? Abdullah bin Omar: So I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is wrong with me? He said: “This is the cross, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from it.”"
"954","954 Amr bin Ali informed us, saying: Yahya, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Maysara, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, that Abdullah, “He saw a man praying with his feet lined up, and he said: You have violated the Sunnah. If you had kept them apart, it would have been better.”"
"955","955 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Maysarah bin Habib told me, he said: I heard the curse. Ibn Amr narrates, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, that he “saw a man who had lined up his feet, and said: He made a mistake in the Sunnah, even if he erred.” Between the two of them, he was astonished to me.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Ubaidah did not hear from his father, and the hadith is good."
"956","956 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, Sufyan said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amara bin al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “had a pause when he began the prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"957","957 Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: I am Jarir, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. He said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began the prayer, he remained quietly silent. I said: May my mother and father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God. Do you say in your silence between the takbir and the recitation? He said: I say: Oh God, distance me from my sins, as You distanced between the East and the West. Oh God, purify me from my sins, just as a white garment is purified from filth. Oh God, wash me away from my sins with ice, water and hail.”"
"958","958 Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed told us, he said: Shuraih bin Yazid Al-Hadrami told us, he said: Shuaib told me, he said: Muhammad bin told me Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when he began the prayer, he said ‘Allahu Akbar’, then he said: ‘My prayer and my rituals are My life and my death belong to God, Lord of the worlds, He has no partner, and with that I was commanded and I am the first of the Muslims. O God, guide me to the best deeds and the best. No one guides to the best of morals except You, and protect me from bad deeds, and no one protects me from bad morals except You.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He is Hadith of a Homsi who returned to Medina, then to Mecca (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"959","959 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Salamah told us, he said: My uncle told me. Al-Majshun bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “When he began the prayer, he said ‘Allahu Akbar’, then he said: I turn my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth, upright, and I am not of The polytheists, my prayer, my rituals, my life, and my death belong to God, Lord of the worlds, He has no partner, and with that I was commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. Oh God, you are The King: There is no god but You. I, Your servant, have wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins. No one forgives sins except You, and guide me. To the best of morals, no one guides to the best of them except You. Avert from me the bad of it. No one can avert the bad of it from me except You. At Your pleasure, Your happiness, and the good. It is all in your hands and evil is not your fault. I am through you and to you, you are blessed and exalted. I seek your forgiveness and I repent to you.”"
"960","960 Ubayd Allah bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq, he said: I am Ja’far bin Sulayman, on the authority of Ali bin Ali, on the authority of my father Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he opened the prayer, he would say: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise.” “Blessed be your name, exalted be your glory, and there is no god but you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"961","961 Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulayman told me, on the authority of Ali bin Ali, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil On the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began prayer at night, he would say: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise. “Blessed be your name, exalted be your glory, and there is no god but you.”"
"962","962 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, Qatada, and Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that he said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “was leading us in prayer when a man came to him and entered the mosque, and he was overcome with emotion and said: God is great, praise be to God.” Many praises, good and blessed. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished his prayer, he said: Which of you spoke some words? So he cursed the people He said: “He did not say anything wrong.” He said: “I, O Messenger of God, came and was moved by my heart, so I said it.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I saw twelve kings hastening to see which of them would raise it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"963","963 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr and Omar begin the recitation with, “Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"964","964 Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “I prayed with The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with Abu Bakr and with Omar, so they opened with praise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"965","965 Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: I am Ali bin Mushar, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Fulfil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “While the Prophet was praying May God bless him and grant him peace. One day while we appeared, he fell asleep, then he raised his head smiling. We said to him: What made you laugh, O Messenger? God? What is wrong with you is the amputee {3} “Then he said: “Do you know what Al-Kawthar is? We said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: For it is a river that my Lord promised me in Paradise. Its vessels are greater than the number of the stars. My nation will return it to me. Then the servant is disturbed by them, and I say: My Lord, he is from my nation, and he says: You do not know what happened after you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"966","966 Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq informed us, saying: I heard my father saying: I am Abu Hamza, on the authority of Mansour bin Zazan, on the authority of Anas bin Malik said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer, but he did not hear us reciting. In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. He led us in prayer.” Abu Bakr and Omar, but we did not hear it from them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"967","967 Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj Abu Saeed told us, he said: Uqba told me, he said: Shua’bah and Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada On the authority of Anas, he said: “I prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman, but I did not hear any of them.” “In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful”"
"968","968 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Uthman told us, and he is Ibn Ghayath, he said: Abu Naama al-Hanafi told me, He said: We are Ibn Abdullah bin Mughaffal. He said: Whenever Abdullah bin Mughaffal heard someone reciting: In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful, he would say: “I prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and behind Abu Bakr, and behind Omar, but I did not hear any of them reciting In the Name of God, Most Gracious.” The Most Merciful"
"969","969 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Rahman, that he heard Abu Al-Sa’ib, the servant of Hisham bin Zahra, saying: I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays a prayer in which he does not recite the Mother of the Qur’an It is prematurity, it is prematurity, it is incomplete prematurity.” So I said: O Abu Hurairah, sometimes I am behind the imam, so he winked at my arm and said: Recite it, O Persian, to yourself, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: God Almighty said: “I divided the prayer between me and My servant is divided into two halves, so half of it is for me, and half of it is for my servant, and my servant is entitled to whatever he asks.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Read what he says.” The servant: Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. God says: My servant praised me. The servant says: The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. God says: My servant praised me. He says Servant: Owner of the Day of Judgment. God says: My servant has glorified Me, and this verse is between Me and My servant, and My servant shall have whatever he asks. Thee we worship and Thee. We seek help. This verse is between Me and My servant, and for My servant whatever he asks. The servant says: Guide us to the straight path {6} The path of those whom You have bestowed. “Not those upon whom anger is incurred, nor those who go astray. {7} So these are for My servant, and for My servant is what he asks.”"
"970","970 Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “There is no prayer for the one who does not recite the Fatihah of the Book.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"971","971 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Al-Samit, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no prayer for the one who does not recite the opening of the book onwards.”"
"972","972 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with us while Gabriel was with him. He heard the opposite above him, so Gabriel raised his gaze to the sky and said: This is a door that has been opened from heaven that has never been opened before. He said: Then an angel descended from it. Then he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “Rejoice about two lights that you have been given that were not given to a prophet before you: the Opener of the Book, and the End of the Book.” Surah Al-Baqarah, you will not recite a letter of it unless you give it to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"973","973 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman, he said: I heard Hafs bin Asim narrates, on the authority of Abu Sa’id bin Al-Mu’alla, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by him while he was praying, so he called him and said: I prayed and then I came to him. He said: “What prevented you from answering me?” I said: I was praying. He said: Didn’t God say: O you who have believed, respond to God and to the Messenger when he calls you to give you life. Shall I not teach you? What is the greatest surah before I leave the mosque? He said: So he went to go out. I said: Yes, O Messenger of God, as you say. He said: Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. These are the seven doubles that I have been given. And the Great Qur’an” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"974","974 Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, saying: I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jafar, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has not revealed anything in the Torah or in the Gospel.” Like the Mother of the Qur’an, which is the seven repeated verses, and it is divided between Me and My servant.”"
"975","975 Muhammad ibn Qudamah informed us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was given seven of the long ones.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"976","976 Ali ibn Hajar al-Marwazi informed us, saying: We have a partner, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in His saying: “Seven of the double ones.” He said: “The seven long ones.”"
"977","977 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Yahya, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara, on the authority of Imran, he said: “The Prophet prayed, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. At noon, a man behind him recited, “Glorify the Name of your Most High Lord.” When he prayed, he said: “Who has recited, Glorify the Name of your Most High Lord?” A man said: “I.” He said: “I have learned that some of you have left me alone.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"978","978 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Abu Awanah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “performed the noon prayer, or the afternoon prayer, and a man was reciting behind him. When he left, he said: Which of you recited Subhanahu `Asma’ Your Lord is the Most High? Then a man from among the people said: I did, and I only intended good with it. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I know that some of you have \"He took it out of me\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"979","979 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ibn Akaimah al-Laythi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he left a prayer in which he recited aloud, and said: “Did any of you recite with me just before?” A man said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: I say: Why should I dispute the Qur’an? He said: The people stopped reciting what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had spoken out loud in reciting from the prayers when they heard that."
"980","980 Hisham bin Ammar informed us, on the authority of Sadaqah, on the authority of Zayd bin Waqid, on the authority of Hazzam bin Hakim, on the authority of Nafi bin Mahmoud bin Rabi’ah. On the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led with us some prayers in which the recitation was recited aloud. He said: “No.” “None of you recites when I recite aloud, except with the Mother of the Qur’an.”"
"981","981 Al-Jaroud bin Muadh told us, he said: Abu Khalid Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The imam has only been appointed to be followed, so when he says “Allahu Akbar,” then “Allahu Akbar.” He recites, so listen, and when he says: God hears those who praise Him, then say: O God, our Lord, to You be praise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"982","982 Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Makhrami told us, he said: Muhammad bin Saad told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ajlan told me, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, On the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The imam is only to be followed, so if he says the greatest, then say the greatest.” And when he recites, listen attentively.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: We do not know that anyone followed Ibn Ajlan, as he said: “And when he recites, listen attentively.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"983","983 Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Zaid bin Hubab told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told us, he said: Abu Al-Zahiriyah Hudayr told me. Ibn Kurayb, he said: Kathir Ibn Murrah Al-Hadrami narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, I heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked, “Is it true? Is there a recitation for every prayer? He said: Yes. A man from the Ansar said: This is obligatory. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to me and I was there. The people approached him and said: “I never see the imam lead the people except that he is sufficient for them.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He succeeded Zayd ibn Hubab, in His saying: “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to me.”"
"984","984 Yusuf bin Issa and Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Musa, he said: We are Mas’ar, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Saskiki, on the authority of Ibn Abi More fully, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I am not able to learn anything from the Qur’an, so teach me something that suffices for it. The Qur’an, he said: Say: “Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is great, and there is no power nor strength except in God,” Abu Abdul Rahman: Ibrahim Al-Saskiski is not that strong. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"985","985 Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Na Baqiya, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, he said: Al-Zuhri informed me, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the reader believes, then they believe, then the angels believe, so whoever agrees to his security is also safe.” The angels forgave him all his previous sins.”"
"986","986 Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “If the reader believes, then they believe, then the angels believe, so whoever’s belief coincides with the belief of the angels, his sins will be forgiven.” He came forward from his sin.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"987","987 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Muammar told me, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When the imam says: Not upon whom is anger nor gone astray, say Amen, for the angels say: Amen. And the imam says: Amen, so whoever’s assurance coincides with the assurance of the angels, his previous sins will be forgiven.”"
"988","988 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id, and Abu Salamah that they informed him, on the authority of Abu Hurairah The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the imam believes and they believe, then whoever whose belief coincides with the belief of the angels will be forgiven.” “Whatever sin he committed”"
"989","989 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “If the imam says: ‘Neither upon whom is Anger nor those who go astray’, say: ‘Ameen’, for whoever’s words agree with the words of the angels will be forgiven.” He will be forgiven for his previous sins.”"
"990","990 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “If one of you says: Amen, and the angels in heaven say: Amen, and one of them agrees with the other, he will be forgiven for his previous deeds.” \"His sin\""
